insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-listing-check', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01 (Logan). The listing check, in Sean's order, and the audit board on the business dashboard. Full detail: CLAUDE.md in lesaruss/vegansexplore-com (Directory review, "The listing check, in Sean's order").

SEAN'S ORDER (2026-11-01): "the first best indicator is Google Maps... If they pass that, they can move on to their website... if it doesn't have the right security, automatic flag, you're going into review... then it's Instagram... a grace of 6 months... a bounty... If they confirm they're open... we flag them for special support." Default taken and approved ("go"): a dead or insecure website goes to review even when Google vouches for the place.

1. GOOGLE. Google says closed: off the Directory (nightly hold, ve_directory_auto_hold); the Monday re-check (ve_closed_recheck_send / _read) puts back any Google shows open again.
2. WEBSITE. Edge function ve-listing-health (migration 20261101_listing_health.sql). Cron ve-listing-health, every 10 minutes 2:00 to 3:50 AM Eastern, 25 a run (about 300 a night; 1,104 local places with a website, so about four nights for the first full pass), each place monthly. Fails: the address no longer exists, nothing answers, 404/410/5xx, a parked or for-sale page, no https, a bad certificate. Passes: 401/403/406/429/503 (a site that turns scanners away, e.g. Kroger and QFC behind Akamai). A timeout or transport error is unknown and read again the next day, never held on one try. Grocery chains (ve-grocery-store) and LESARUSS.ai listings are left out. No website at all is Google's job.
3. INSTAGRAM, only when the website failed (Apify instagram-profile-scraper, handles batched; about a quarter cent each). A post within 180 days passes and flags the place for support (its website needs fixing). No post, no account or private: held (On hold, details.review.by = Listing check, the reasons) and a 50-point, 30-day "Is it still open?" bounty goes up in its chapter's still-open-<chapter> campaign (ve_listing_still_open_bounty, made if missing).
4. AFTER. Held places are read weekly and come back on their own when they pass. A member's bounty visit settles it (ve-bounties applyCheck); found open means back on the Directory and ve_listing_support_flag. Claimed or owned listings, and ones put back by hand within 90 days (review_ok_until), are never held, only flagged.
DATA. ve_listing_health (one row per listing: web_status ok|blocked|down|insecure|none|unknown, web_detail, https_ok, ig_handle, ig_status, ig_last_post, verdict, reasons, held_at, support_at/why/done_at, history). Actions: sweep (cron or ops), one {slug, save}, support, support_done {listing_id}.
DEPOT. Directory review > Needs support: each place with why, Done and Open.
PROVEN 2026-11-01. Chi Chi Vegan Taco Shop: dead domain, last Instagram post January 2024, held with its Atlanta bounty. Happy Zoe Vegan Bakery: broken certificate, posting this week, left on and flagged for support. Twelve sample listings passed.
THE AUDIT BOARD ON THE DASHBOARD (Sean: "use that mechanism that we use for BCPS Marcom... one that has passed the audit and one that hasn't"). ve-partner-dashboard.js healthCard / healthBlock: the Audit view opens with Your listing check, each check grouped by area (Google, Website, Instagram, Your Directory page) as passed, flagged or check, what we found and the fix, a score, On the Directory or In review, and What happens next. Sample at /business/sample?tab=brand&pd=audit: Green Leaf Kitchen passes 8 of 8, Corner Sprout Cafe (made up) In review at 1 of 8 (healthSamples in business/sample/listing-demo.js).
NOT DONE. The live board on a real owner's dashboard (D.health) is not wired. Needs support was not opened in a browser (admin sign-in); its API answers.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-listing-check' and body like 'BUILD RECORD, 2026-11-01%');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-listing-check', 'vegans-explore', 'Logan', $pb$OPEN QUESTION, 2026-11-01 (Sean, to answer first in the next chat). "What if on the partner dashboard they had a score based off of this? If we're already running these scans on these businesses... we're just capturing the results. So when somebody unlocks their claim, they get access to this information, all designed to support them, and it lets them know exactly what to do, with a button: do you want us to fix these issues? It takes them down the path to our monthly services. It all starts with them getting their audit. That's what we're saying in the Restaurant Guide and the Entrepreneur Guide: they're unlocking their profile and seeing everything that's there. We could also feed opportunities directly into their dashboard. And the dashboard on that profile becomes their dashboard, plus a few other things that aren't in that profile. What are your thoughts?" Status: not answered yet; no build until Sean says go.$pb$, 'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-listing-check' and body like 'OPEN QUESTION, 2026-11-01%');
